#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/id #uuid "3d38f3e0-4c27-5ac6-ac16-9c8f57e0000e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4327" :question/problem "Find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-1,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1,5,-2 \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{6} \\right) \\approx 111.9^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105512 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/id #uuid "d6d1be58-7321-50ca-a47d-5e80d55277c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4328" :question/problem "Find $\\angle BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,-5)$, $B(-1,0,-4)$, and $C(5,1,1).$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,-5⟩,\\,b=⟨-1,0,-4⟩,\\,c=⟨5,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $\\angle BAC = \\theta.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-4⟩-⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩-⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{11}\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}} \\right) \\approx 92.5^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105529 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/id #uuid "fb2df468-d70d-5300-8860-0cb729cb13c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5112" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle t, \\, -2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 6, \\, t \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-4 \\\\ t\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot t & =-4 \\\\ 6t-2t & =-4 \\\\ 4t & =-4 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨-1,-2⟩,\\,b=⟨6,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{37}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{185}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{4}{\\sqrt{185}} \\right) \\approx 107.1^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e024ed6-1a55-553c-8b31-a1f0be181613" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{83.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305568} {:answer/id #uuid "f463ce5d-e874-561f-9179-cadc61ce1062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{74.1}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305569} {:answer/id #uuid "665a91cf-af8d-5f29-b375-55e8c4fd87a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{69.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305570} {:answer/id #uuid "11c741ef-936e-5a40-8cb0-491147a382b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79.8}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305571} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c647c8-1a16-534c-ae50-9ef7e11dcc32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{71.1}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f463ce5d-e874-561f-9179-cadc61ce1062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{74.1}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305569} :answer-field/id #uuid "184001aa-6c2f-5e00-8950-8028d8aa6399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0153efd-ca23-5fc7-9bdf-30cbb73efaf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-101502" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨7,2⟩$ and $b=⟨0,6⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{53}\\cdot \\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{53}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{53}})≈{74.1}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb1e08c5-8191-51cb-828c-4e1bf4d18edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269075} {:answer/id #uuid "c48d61db-8a7b-58a9-baa3-b45f0e2b2e24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{77}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269076} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe43b6a-8e20-5aa9-b47c-1e0b409544b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{86}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269077} {:answer/id #uuid "a8481d0e-1847-5899-a263-24206ff622f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{91}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269078} {:answer/id #uuid "f68369eb-d5b2-597a-8ad3-4e02ef54893c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fe43b6a-8e20-5aa9-b47c-1e0b409544b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{86}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269077} :answer-field/id #uuid "4237779a-fb1d-5aae-9935-ca22c819fe5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16a09fd3-be95-51b4-b0ac-0c24039ae9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-101511" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,1)$, $B(3,1,-2)$, and $C(-1,1,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,1,-2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,1,-2⟩-⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,2,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,1⟩-⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{182}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{182}})≈{86}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe092e6a-a292-562a-8e10-3a18cf911c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{150}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305575} {:answer/id #uuid "9012605f-9225-5ab8-adaf-c6233a381fab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305576} {:answer/id #uuid "cd96dcf2-df7b-5d7d-b63a-2f885d7a0ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305577} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c459a6-1bf4-521f-b918-6d61ed3c3273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305578} {:answer/id #uuid "5a531894-930d-5aa8-be0a-b7eeb2655660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6c459a6-1bf4-521f-b918-6d61ed3c3273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305578} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7d14433-e6bf-53f2-aba4-b6c9efded31e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fe38227-7ce9-5330-a6c3-677c59d25bae" :question/math-academy-id "q-101512" :question/problem "Given that $a\\cdot b=-5$, find the angle between $a=⟨2t,t⟩$ and $b=⟨1,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $a\\cdot b=-5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-5 \\\\ 2t\\cdot 1+t\\cdot 3 & =-5 \\\\ 2t+3t & =-5 \\\\ 5t & =-5 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨2(-1),\\,(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{5\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={135}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33d889d7-3053-5698-b65c-fe5ae9aa07f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75.22}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269089} {:answer/id #uuid "bf85c120-7483-5553-bdcd-a44069470789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{78.55}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269090} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6a7436-5d40-5ead-afe9-8fc3f33b83ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{70.99}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269091} {:answer/id #uuid "08336714-fd00-56fc-9883-ef766d26fd89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269092} {:answer/id #uuid "7934f66e-abaa-5481-ab13-a79e21a04132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80.44}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7934f66e-abaa-5481-ab13-a79e21a04132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80.44}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269093} :answer-field/id #uuid "69c601c3-8547-5f8b-8af3-b0698702489b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8fc7cf1b-c116-59a4-83f2-94ca1412ae63" :question/math-academy-id "q-101520" :question/problem "Consider the points $D(t,5,3)$, $E({t}^{2},2,t)$ and $F(t+3,{t}^{2},1).$ Find $∠EDF$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=6.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $D$, $E$, $F$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d=⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩,\\,e=⟨{t}^{2},\\,2,\\,t⟩,\\,f=⟨t+3,\\,{t}^{2},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△DEF$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠EDF=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/c9cfb3e84e6f76d243125f2a09246b2a1300a0134e71359bb2b528082f064f93.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,2,\\,t⟩-⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2}-t,\\,-3,\\,t-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =⟨t+3,\\,{t}^{2},\\,1⟩-⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,{t}^{2}-5,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=6$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =6 \\\\ ({t}^{2}-t)\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot ({t}^{2}-5)+(t-3)\\cdot (-2) & =6 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-3t-3{t}^{2}+15-2t+6 & =6 \\\\ -5t+21 & =6 \\\\ -5t & =-15 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨{3}^{2}-3,-3,3-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-3,0⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨3,{3}^{2}-5,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,4,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}}{|\\overset{\\to }{DE}||\\overset{\\to }{DF}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{29}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{145}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{145}})≈{80.44}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c716782a-b97a-58c3-aa44-b66192a533c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{53}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305582} {:answer/id #uuid "deb98318-2cd0-59c5-8f0f-fb8177d23a14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{48}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305583} {:answer/id #uuid "98e25aad-57ef-55a6-89e1-0626f079d3e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305584} {:answer/id #uuid "5864358b-e236-53ba-b047-be2a74903070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305585} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef2feb2-578c-5cf5-aa04-624fa071db91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ef2feb2-578c-5cf5-aa04-624fa071db91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305586} :answer-field/id #uuid "10fb002f-9c68-5e0d-8422-8879351ebc22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b08cdc2-93c5-5479-9a26-db3836e3a1c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-124802" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨3,1,1⟩$ and $b=⟨1,3,1⟩.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{11}\\cdot \\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{11})≈{50}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e66664f5-380e-5745-be2c-90ad323f2dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{46}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279160} {:answer/id #uuid "0714c6d5-fa2e-5d2a-b410-9cc7f6f50f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{41}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279161} {:answer/id #uuid "726f5315-901e-5c3f-a2a2-290b90bc03b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{38}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279162} {:answer/id #uuid "bdc7251c-e514-5ea7-bf1a-270ab49b97f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279163} {:answer/id #uuid "0adb7bb9-01cb-5473-8b8b-f7b52effa7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0714c6d5-fa2e-5d2a-b410-9cc7f6f50f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{41}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279161} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f5b0741-3fca-5a95-8d71-75222a5d3195" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2793518d-ad57-5b32-92b4-c966424db7d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-124813" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,2)$, $B(3,-5,1)$, and $C(1,-4,-1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,2⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-5,1⟩,\\,c=⟨1,-4,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-5,1⟩-⟨2,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-4,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨1,-4,-1⟩-⟨2,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{18}\\cdot \\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3\\sqrt{38}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{14}{3\\sqrt{38}})≈{41}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b799d246-a11b-5070-8463-6dd43a31f2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{23}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305589} {:answer/id #uuid "0efd139f-2138-5c6a-8e89-f0113b4b5529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305590} {:answer/id #uuid "5e90994a-68d7-554e-8846-e8e826dcaf09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305591} {:answer/id #uuid "77dbf72a-adae-5231-b827-7a1763244fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305592} {:answer/id #uuid "a49f55ad-0b4a-59d1-9d05-998e90849253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0efd139f-2138-5c6a-8e89-f0113b4b5529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305590} :answer-field/id #uuid "45442419-9910-5c12-9801-3473e30f7e7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2da436d8-ed5e-54f6-ba9e-01977eb421f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-124826" :question/problem "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-2,1,0)$, $Y(-1,0,4)$, and $Z(-1,2,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-2,1,0⟩,\\,y=⟨-1,0,4⟩,\\,z=⟨-1,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,0⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,4⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{40}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{240}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{4\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}})={25}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "981c0757-fe53-59c1-96f1-1e7b765c291c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102424} {:answer/id #uuid "c5f14e2e-cbcf-5479-8070-9329dd4c6100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102425} {:answer/id #uuid "e8e95d0e-98cd-57c8-91db-15c16b7abcf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102426} {:answer/id #uuid "04911650-f394-5f92-89c4-a8ad3def4fe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102427} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac0780e-b0e2-5eaf-baa3-7b52daaa8a34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8e95d0e-98cd-57c8-91db-15c16b7abcf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102426} :answer-field/id #uuid "31367477-0f1a-5ca5-9bf8-a56c2f82c41e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fefdea41-9260-5cb7-a494-74f9e1519448" :question/math-academy-id "q-19035" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨3,2,1⟩$ and $b=⟨1,2,3⟩.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{14} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{5}{7})≈{44}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8afbfb09-b22c-5fb4-ad63-9b272b5b0f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{74.66}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269110} {:answer/id #uuid "8963ce6a-0bfd-5fd2-b165-d792ada55b90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{82.28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269111} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6a8900-1583-5035-b877-a331a777d7a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79.76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269112} {:answer/id #uuid "5826b01a-a2bb-59f5-97f6-55db95fe21e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{94.32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269113} {:answer/id #uuid "6745ac4a-89a9-5753-84d7-9c7d0584dc63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6745ac4a-89a9-5753-84d7-9c7d0584dc63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269114} :answer-field/id #uuid "a854aaae-2f37-5309-b178-44153a0fe3f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de2bc7db-4647-58f0-bdd4-89b0098b6ec1" :question/math-academy-id "q-19036" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨4,-3,2⟩$ and $b=⟨3,4,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{29}\\cdot \\sqrt{26}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{754}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{754}})≈{85.82}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7ae5663-0d59-5cf2-a70b-62b42701ed37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{87.33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305596} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c57a36-dbd9-5114-a664-b21e93edfecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88.21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305597} {:answer/id #uuid "28c08126-cfd7-5626-9ae8-efab8abd2d87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81.33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305598} {:answer/id #uuid "65a41328-671f-5e00-8c6d-3e0ed7c56e07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{72.34}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305599} {:answer/id #uuid "46a9a117-bce4-54bb-952d-4a280afe930e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{67.13}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28c08126-cfd7-5626-9ae8-efab8abd2d87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81.33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305598} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c8876ef-878d-5529-9fcb-4f967104239f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "854d0f4a-8e08-5dc7-a816-ea56cbf65d2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-19040" :question/problem "Given that $g\\cdot h=8$, find the angle between $g=⟨t,t,t-1⟩$ and $h=⟨4,-2,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, since $g\\cdot h=8$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =8 \\\\ t\\cdot 4+t\\cdot (-2)+(t-1)\\cdot (-1) & =8 \\\\ 4t-2t-t+1 & =8 \\\\ t+1 & =8 \\\\ t & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g & =⟨7,7,7-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,7,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $g$ and $h$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{g\\cdot h}{|\\,g\\,||\\,h\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{g}_{x}{h}_{x}+{g}_{y}{h}_{y}+{g}_{z}{h}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{g}_{x}^{2}+{g}_{y}^{2}+{g}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{h}_{x}^{2}+{h}_{y}^{2}+{h}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{134}\\cdot \\sqrt{21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2\\,814}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2\\,814}})≈{81.33}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106032 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aca6bd26-6933-59e2-8800-0702ffaaee5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102430} {:answer/id #uuid "b59b3837-6fdf-509f-b5ae-fc2925a1d015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102431} {:answer/id #uuid "bd485a1b-1304-5ab4-ac9e-8d4a2f9d2b36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102432} {:answer/id #uuid "08d4a2e8-a01f-5019-a296-05c07d911af5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102433} {:answer/id #uuid "673c1a77-a57c-5bbd-8e96-8088500a00a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08d4a2e8-a01f-5019-a296-05c07d911af5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102433} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2546906-9052-54aa-8870-1c81e7a0a86b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6f80f82-94f9-5bde-ac4d-44929ef66109" :question/math-academy-id "q-19110" :question/problem "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(0,4,5)$, $Q(1,5,4)$, and $R(2,3,6).$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨0,4,5⟩,\\,q=⟨1,5,4⟩,\\,r=⟨2,3,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨1,5,4⟩-⟨0,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨2,3,6⟩-⟨0,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0)={90}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "939952d1-0149-556b-a88e-f0b50063c995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "102^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102436} {:answer/id #uuid "d96db57b-61cd-5adc-9c38-4cb9988be22f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102437} {:answer/id #uuid "0341b012-c894-5a3e-8faf-ee417a81b04f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102438} {:answer/id #uuid "10dd6f82-5f13-59a8-9a02-f812afe863b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "51^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102439} {:answer/id #uuid "7bed2b44-02ab-5ef6-9f67-769273a601a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10dd6f82-5f13-59a8-9a02-f812afe863b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "51^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102439} :answer-field/id #uuid "9777b9d4-0c7d-5416-9108-e56715ea430c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "adc865e5-b770-53c4-be9e-d693f63bd5dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-19112" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(3,-3,1)$, $B(5,-3,3)$, and $C(3,-2,3).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨3,-3,1⟩,\\,b=⟨5,-3,3⟩,\\,c=⟨3,-2,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨5,-3,3⟩-⟨3,-3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,3⟩-⟨3,-3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}})≈{51}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e5a51c2-e9bf-5c21-8013-39f0e3fa4759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305603} {:answer/id #uuid "358ce25e-1f9a-5d75-a188-9f42822339ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{47.1}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305604} {:answer/id #uuid "b14bb041-b382-5f3d-8807-92d5f00ce59c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{42.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305605} {:answer/id #uuid "ba3edf31-f02d-5254-8005-709d848b9be1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{31.7}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305606} {:answer/id #uuid "f8b7063b-2074-5d0d-a432-d3066324f253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35.6}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8b7063b-2074-5d0d-a432-d3066324f253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35.6}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305607} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc72ad0a-0b50-5030-9cfb-302e160d3622" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aca4f040-eb16-55f8-9cf3-b8f2b415e794" :question/math-academy-id "q-67797" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨-1,7,0⟩$ and $b=⟨3,6,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 3+7\\cdot 6+0\\cdot (-1)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{7}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{\\sqrt{50}\\cdot \\sqrt{46}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{\\sqrt{2300}} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{10\\sqrt{23}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{39}{10\\sqrt{23}})≈{35.6}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb9d024a-612a-5b88-b561-2eca5dd12c41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269152} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee2a05a-ca70-5223-ba9e-36cd6fa08e55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269153} {:answer/id #uuid "6eaac85c-277b-51f1-baf6-a4d8434347b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269154} {:answer/id #uuid "a4eef7ee-ce27-568c-aa25-74f1486ec107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269155} {:answer/id #uuid "3f8ec3a5-7e51-5c63-9ee0-131bcdf218d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f8ec3a5-7e51-5c63-9ee0-131bcdf218d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269156} :answer-field/id #uuid "89db74db-3d63-59f5-b41d-544e3f33dabd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61191758-28d5-55a6-95f0-ed679272a908" :question/math-academy-id "q-77164" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(3t,t,4),$ $B(3t,4t,3)$ and $C(5t,t+1,5).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩,\\,b=⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3t,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2$, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =2 \\\\ 0\\cdot 2t+3t\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 3t-1 & =2 \\\\ 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨0,3,-1⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}})≈{75}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305608 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d72837a-6c83-5f35-929e-ffa5344f19be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63.43}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305610} {:answer/id #uuid "f974f885-0f17-5500-a7fe-b3bd99079839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{21.42}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305611} {:answer/id #uuid "c52c118f-55a2-5a15-92a7-015727f1d9f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{77.07}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305612} {:answer/id #uuid "38a10d4d-48eb-58bc-ab1d-69d971c1060c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{26.57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305613} {:answer/id #uuid "be57eafa-5a3e-5467-8488-646d3a30fbca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10.52}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38a10d4d-48eb-58bc-ab1d-69d971c1060c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{26.57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305613} :answer-field/id #uuid "43f81a4f-4f23-590d-a87a-a991a42d8c5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e36ca8d6-b65d-5cd3-83a7-070f0b3504a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-77167" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(2t,4,3),$ $B(5t-1,4,3)$ and $C(2t+4,t+5,3).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=8.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩,\\,b=⟨5t-1,\\,4,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨2t+4,\\,t+5,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨5t-1,\\,4,\\,3⟩-⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3t-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨2t+4,\\,t+5,\\,3⟩-⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,t+1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=8,$ we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =8 \\\\ (3t-1)\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (t+1)+0\\cdot 0 & =8 \\\\ 4(3t-1)+0+0 & =8 \\\\ 12t-4 & =8 \\\\ 12t & =12 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,0,0⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{80}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}})≈{26.57}^{∘}.\n$$"}]}
